{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/resistanceDistance(from:to:tolerance:maxIterations:)"},"sections":[],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/spectralgraphtheory\/graphprotocols\/graph\/resistancedistance(from:to:tolerance:maxiterations:)"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"resistanceDistance","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"from","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"source","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"to","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"target","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"tolerance","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Double","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" = 1e-10, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"maxIterations","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"? = nil) ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"NoConvergence","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/NoConvergence","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols13NoConvergenceV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Double","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Conjugate gradients on the Laplacian grounded at ","type":"text"},{"code":"target","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", from 0, until the residual’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Euclidean norm is at most ","type":"text"},{"code":"tolerance","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (relative to the right-hand side, which has norm 1),","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"or, on a weight spread that puts that below rounding, until the true residual stops","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"improving. Jacobi preconditioned for 300 iterations, then by a modified incomplete Cholesky","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"factor in maximum-spanning-tree order. O((n + m) √κ) time; about 9 n words, and O(n + m) for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the factor when it is built.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"style":"note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"source"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"target"},{"type":"text","text":" are vertices of the graph, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tolerance > 0"},{"type":"text","text":", and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxIterations"},{"type":"text","text":", when given, is at least 1."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Precondition","type":"aside"},{"style":"note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NoConvergence"},{"type":"text","text":" after "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxIterations"},{"type":"text","text":" conjugate-gradient iterations (one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"matrix–vector product each; 20,000 + 2n when nil), with that count and the residual’s norm"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"relative to the right-hand side’s. No input has reached the default limit in the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"measurements."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Throws","type":"aside"}],"kind":"content"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The resistance distance between ","type":"text"},{"code":"source","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"target","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (Klein and Randić 1993): the effective","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"resistance between them when each edge is a conductance (its weight; 1 without ","type":"text"},{"code":"weight:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"),","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(e_s − e_t)ᵀ L⁺ (e_s − e_t). 0 when they are the same vertex, without reading any weight;","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"nil when they lie in different components. Symmetric. To read weights as resistances","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"instead, pass ","type":"text"},{"code":"{ 1 \/ r($0) }","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory","doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"metadata":{"externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P08SpectralA6TheoryE18resistanceDistance4from2to9tolerance13maxIterationsSdSg6VertexQz_ALSdSiSgtAA13NoConvergenceVYKF","modules":[{"name":"SpectralGraphTheory","relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"]}],"roleHeading":"Instance Method","extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","title":"resistanceDistance(from:to:tolerance:maxIterations:)","symbolKind":"method","remoteSource":{"fileName":"ElectricalNetworks.swift","url":"https